m play the bottom of his deck. It turns out it is a Lightning Slash which hits Kagaara. That would be all Tempest does on the Legacy/Captain Cosmic/Tempest chain except...</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; That triggers Warfang&#39;s Mindbreaker retaliation. It is 2 damage out to every target on the board due to her other title and a couple of Captain Cosmic&#39;s constructs are already sitting at two health. We resolve the Mindbreaker attack against all the villain targets, however the Legacy/Captain Cosmic/Tempest/Warfang chain isn&#39;t done because...</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; That triggers Tempest&#39;s Dynamic Syphon given to him by Captain Cosmic which he uses to activate Cleansing Downpour, healing all the hero for two damage. We finish that, the last step in the Legacy/Captain Cosmic/Tempest/Warfang/Tempest chain. This step is resolved.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Warfang finishes her Mindbreaker attack. That step is resolved.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&gt;&gt;&gt; Tempest already finished his Lightning Slash attack, so that was already resolved.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&gt;&gt; Captain Cosmic does his third attack via Autonomous Blade. That step is resolved.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&gt; Legacy gets to draw and end his turn, that step is resolved.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The ziggurat is complete and I explain to my boyfriend how that happened all on Legacy&#39;s turn on the car ride home. The Absolute Zero player at the table seriously considers a &quot;no shenanigans&quot; rule for future games.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Oh yeah. There was an Absolute Zero player.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>I love this game. Heh. As ever, feel free to share also convoluted stories you&#39;ve had.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>(Edit: Corrected where the Seeker Title went.)</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div>",
